{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Leo, I'm sorry you've had to ask twice. I checked your laptop (BL-LT-0106) and the cause is clear: the disk is almost full, with only 3.5% (about 9 GB) free. That stops files from saving. Please try these steps: 1) Empty your Recycle Bin and clear your Downloads folder. 2) Open Settings, then System, then Storage, then Temporary files, and remove the temporary files and old Windows Update files. 3) If you use OneDrive, turn on Files On-Demand so synced files stay in the cloud until you open them. 4) Uninstall any apps you no longer need. Then restart the laptop and reply to this ticket. I'll re-check the disk. If it is still under 10% free after cleanup, we'll look at a larger drive or a replacement laptop.",
  "internal_note": "Reported: laptop cannot save files, repeat request, P3. Checked lookup_user: Leo Martins (user 6, Sales), account active, not locked, no failed logins, mailbox 26% used, device BL-LT-0106. check_device_status: online, last check-in 2026-10-11 02:58 UTC, disk 256 GB total, 9 GB free (3.5%), low disk space warning. Matches KB-017 symptoms. Cleanup is user-side and cannot be run remotely from here, so the user was given the KB-017 fix steps. Next: after the user confirms cleanup, re-run check_device_status. Escalate to Tier 2 (replacement or larger drive) if free space is still under 10%. Also check KB-019 if slowness persists after cleanup. No account actions taken.",
